# SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000134  -  CAT II
# The web server must set an inactive timeout for sessions.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000295-WSR-000134
group:           V-206415
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-002361
control_rev5:    AC-12

contribution:    Splunk closes an idle session from its own settings: web.conf
                 tools.sessions.timeout is the inactivity period after which the Splunk Web
                 session expires, and ui_inactivity_timeout must not be set below 1, which
                 would stop the inactivity notification firing at all.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout present
check:           web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout max 5
check:           web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout min 2
check:           web.conf [settings] ui_inactivity_timeout min 1
check:           web.conf [settings] ui_inactivity_timeout max 10
check:           server.conf [general] sessionTimeout matches ^(([1-9]|1[0-5])m|([1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|[1-8][0-9]{2}|900)s)$
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/manage-users/configure-user-session-timeouts
vendor:          web.conf [settings] ui_inactivity_timeout https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/manage-users/configure-user-session-timeouts
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The organization's risk categorization of the hosted application decides
                 which tier in the check text applies; the product STIG's 15 minutes
                 satisfies the low- and medium-risk tiers and the application cannot
                 determine its own categorization.
external:        A fronting proxy or SSO gateway with its own idle timer must also close
                 idle sessions, and that timer is not an application setting.
external:        The product STIG scopes SPLK-CL-000010 to the search head.

citation:        ui_inactivity_timeout max 15 and ui_inactivity_timeout present are
                 removed. The number 15 is the product STIG's value for a different key -
                 the fix for SPLK-CL-000010 sets tools.session.timeout = 15 and touches
                 nothing else - while ui_inactivity_timeout's documented default is 60
                 (web.conf.spec:403-410), so a max of 15 on that key reports a finding
                 against an instance configured exactly as the benchmark authority
                 prescribes, and present penalizes a default that does not defeat the
                 requirement. The check text's own numbers (5, 10 and 20 minutes by
                 application risk tier) are a bound on the idle close time, not on this
                 notification interval, so transplanting any of them to
                 ui_inactivity_timeout would be the same error with better provenance. min
                 1 is kept because it is the one setting of this key that defeats the
                 requirement outright: below 1 "Sessions stay alive for as long as the
                 browser is open" (web.conf.spec:408-409). tools.sessions.timeout keeps
                 present and max 15 from the product STIG check ("missing or ... 16 or
                 more"), which is inside even the strictest 5-minute tier's parent
                 requirement, plus the specification's floor of 2 (web.conf.spec:929-930).
finding:         Splunk Web does not close idle sessions within the period the
                 application's risk tier allows: web.conf [settings] tools.sessions.timeout
                 is unset or 16 or more minutes, or ui_inactivity_timeout is below 1 so the
                 inactivity notification never fires.
